## 3. Contention — More Threads on Hot Rows = LOWER Throughput

**❌ NEVER: Scale concurrency on hot-row workloads expecting higher throughput**

With N concurrent writers on the same row:
- Only 1 can commit per "round" (the winner)
- The other N-1 are aborted with 40001 and must retry
- Wasted work = (N-1)/N of all attempts
- 5 threads: ~80% waste → 20 threads: ~95% waste
- **TPS goes DOWN as you add more pods/threads**

**✅ ALWAYS: Eliminate the hot row or reduce contention**

```sql
-- GOOD: Atomic single-statement update — no read-modify-write contention
UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance + 75.00 WHERE account_id = $1;

-- GOOD: Use SELECT FOR UPDATE to serialize access explicitly
BEGIN;
SELECT balance FROM accounts WHERE account_id = $1 FOR UPDATE;
UPDATE accounts SET balance = $new_balance WHERE account_id = $1;
COMMIT;
```

Other solutions for hot-row workloads:
- **Shard the account** across multiple rows (e.g., balance sharding)
- **Queue and batch** — collect writes, apply in periodic single-writer batch
- **Reduce transaction scope** — fewer statements = shorter conflict window

> Docs: https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/stable/performance-best-practices-overview#transaction-contention

