## 7. Transaction Size Limits — 16MB Payload Cap

CockroachDB has a ~16MB limit on **total transaction payload** (not just individual rows). This applies to the SUM of all writes in a single transaction.

**❌ NEVER: Write many KB-sized rows in a single transaction**

```
-- BAD: 25 statements × 500KB each = 12.5MB. 30 × 600KB = 18MB → EXCEEDS LIMIT
-- Error: "split failed while applying backpressure to Put"
BEGIN;
INSERT INTO audit_log (...) VALUES (...);  -- 500KB
INSERT INTO audit_log (...) VALUES (...);  -- 500KB
... × 25 more times ...
COMMIT;
```

**✅ ALWAYS: Keep transactions under 4MB total, rows under 1MB**

```sql
-- GOOD: Commit every 5-10 statements
-- Batch 1
BEGIN;
INSERT INTO audit_log (...) VALUES (...);  -- statements 1-5
COMMIT;
-- Batch 2
BEGIN;
INSERT INTO audit_log (...) VALUES (...);  -- statements 6-10
COMMIT;
```

**Size guidelines:**
| Target | Limit |
|--------|-------|
| Individual row size | < 1 MB |
| Total transaction payload | < 4 MB |
| Statements per transaction | < 10 |
| Large document storage | Object storage (S3/GCS) with DB reference |
| Document chunking | 64-256 KB per chunk row |

When the 16MB limit is exceeded, `split failed while applying backpressure to Put` occurs because:
1. Large Raft proposals block consensus on every replica
2. Range splits stall while large writes are in-flight
3. LSM compaction falls behind under sustained large writes

> Docs: https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/stable/architecture/distribution-layer#range-splits

