## 11. Multi-Region Table Localities

CockroachDB is the only SQL database with SQL-level data placement control. No PostgreSQL/Oracle equivalent exists.

| Locality | Best For | Read Latency | Write Latency |
|----------|----------|-------------|---------------|
| `REGIONAL BY TABLE` | Data accessed from one primary region | Low in primary | Low in primary |
| `REGIONAL BY ROW` | Data partitioned by user/region | Low from local region | Low to local region |
| `GLOBAL` | Reference data read everywhere | Low everywhere | High (all regions agree) |

```sql
-- Set up regions
ALTER DATABASE mydb PRIMARY REGION 'us-east-1';
ALTER DATABASE mydb ADD REGION 'us-west-2';
ALTER DATABASE mydb ADD REGION 'eu-west-1';

-- Survival goal: survive entire region failure (requires 3+ regions)
ALTER DATABASE mydb SURVIVE REGION FAILURE;

-- Reference/config tables: fast reads everywhere
ALTER TABLE countries SET LOCALITY GLOBAL;

-- Per-user data: each row in its region
ALTER TABLE user_profiles SET LOCALITY REGIONAL BY ROW;

-- Regional operations data (default)
ALTER TABLE transactions SET LOCALITY REGIONAL BY TABLE IN PRIMARY REGION;
```

For `REGIONAL BY ROW` tables, filter by `crdb_region` for locality-optimized reads:

```sql
-- GOOD: Reads served from local replica
SELECT * FROM user_profiles WHERE crdb_region = 'us-east-1' AND user_id = $1;
```

> Docs: https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/stable/multiregion-overview

