## 12. CockroachDB vs PostgreSQL Compatibility

| PostgreSQL | CockroachDB Equivalent |
|-----------|----------------------|
| `uuid_generate_v4()` | `gen_random_uuid()` (built-in, no extension) |
| `SERIAL` / `BIGSERIAL` | `UUID DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()` (SERIAL works but creates hotspots) |
| `LISTEN` / `NOTIFY` | Changefeeds (`CREATE CHANGEFEED FOR TABLE ...`) |
| Advisory locks | Explicit locking or app-level coordination |
| `pg_trgm` extension | `ILIKE` or full-text search with `to_tsvector`/`to_tsquery` |
| PostGIS | Built-in spatial types (`GEOMETRY`, `GEOGRAPHY`) |
| Transactional DDL | Background jobs (one DDL per implicit transaction) |
| `PL/pgSQL` | Supported with some limitations for UDFs/stored procs |
| Temp tables | Supported with `SET experimental_enable_temp_tables = 'on'` |
| `COPY FROM` | Supported for data import |
| `EXPLAIN` format | CockroachDB uses its own plan format |

