## 13. Query Patterns

```sql
-- ✅ ALWAYS use LIMIT on exploratory queries
SELECT * FROM large_table LIMIT 100;

-- ✅ Prefer UPSERT over INSERT ... ON CONFLICT when replacing entire rows
UPSERT INTO accounts (id, name, balance) VALUES ($1, $2, $3);

-- ✅ Use RETURNING to avoid a separate SELECT after writes
INSERT INTO orders (customer_id, amount)
VALUES ($1, $2) RETURNING order_id, created_at;

-- ✅ Use AS OF SYSTEM TIME for follower reads (multi-region latency reduction)
SELECT * FROM accounts AS OF SYSTEM TIME '-10s' WHERE region = 'us-east-1';

-- ✅ Use IMPORT or COPY for bulk data loading (not row-by-row INSERT)
-- ✅ Avoid SELECT * — specify only needed columns
-- ✅ Use CTEs (WITH clauses) — they are supported and optimized
-- ✅ Window functions are fully supported
```

