## 15. EXPLAIN for Performance Analysis

```sql
-- Basic plan (no execution)
EXPLAIN SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id = $1;

-- Actual execution with timing and row counts
EXPLAIN ANALYZE SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id = $1;

-- Verbose with column details
EXPLAIN (VERBOSE) SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id = $1;

-- Distributed execution plan across nodes
EXPLAIN (DISTSQL) SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id = $1;
```

**Red flags in EXPLAIN output:**
| Pattern | Problem | Fix |
|---------|---------|-----|
| `scan` without index | Full table scan | Add an index on the filter column |
| `filter` after `scan` | Post-scan filtering | Add index to push filter into scan |
| `hash join` | May indicate missing index | Add index on join column |
| `sort` without index | Sort not using index | Add index matching ORDER BY |

**Good patterns:**
- `lookup join` — using index for join
- `merge join` — both sides ordered
- `constrained scan` — index limiting scan range

> Docs: https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/stable/performance-recipes#hot-ranges

