## Consolidated Anti-Pattern Quick Reference

| ❌ Anti-Pattern | Why It's Dangerous | ✅ Fix |
|---|---|---|
| SERIAL / SEQUENCE primary keys | Write hotspot on one node, CPU skew | UUID with `gen_random_uuid()` |
| SAVEPOINT-based retry on 40001 | CockroachDB aborts entire txn | Full-transaction retry loop |
| Adding threads to hot-row workloads | More retries = lower TPS | Eliminate hot row or shard |
| Read + write in same long transaction | Holds write intents, increases 40001 | AS OF SYSTEM TIME read → short write |
| Row-by-row INSERT/UPDATE loop (N+1) | N round trips, ~50% idle time | Batch or multi-row statements |
| SELECT * without WHERE/LIMIT in txn | Full table scan, blocks other txns | Add WHERE + LIMIT + indexes |
| 20+ statements in one transaction | Accumulates toward 16MB limit | Commit every 5-10 statements |
| Storing multi-MB JSON/blobs inline | Slow Raft, range split backpressure | Object storage + DB reference |
| Multiple DDL in BEGIN/COMMIT | Not atomic, partial commit risk | One DDL per implicit transaction |
| SELECT * in prepared statements | Schema changes break cached plans | Explicit column lists always |
| Missing STORING on secondary indexes | Index join penalty (extra round trip) | Add STORING for returned columns |
| No GIN index on queried JSONB column | Full-table scan on every JSON query | CREATE INVERTED INDEX |
| Missing retry logic for 40001 | Lost transactions under contention | Retry with exponential backoff + jitter |
| No session guardrails in dev/test | Runaway queries go undetected | SET transaction_rows_read/written_err |
